## Session Structure

### 1. Planning Phase
```markdown
Executive Agent:
- Define strategic goals
- Outline success criteria
- Set implementation priorities

Project Architect:
- Create technical approach
- Define system components
- Identify integration points

All Agents:
- Review and provide input
- Identify potential issues
- Suggest improvements

Human Coordinator:
- Review direction
- Provide guidance
- Approve approach
```

### 2. Design Phase
```markdown
Project Architect:
- Design system components
- Create interface specifications
- Define data models

Security Expert:
- Perform threat modeling
- Identify security requirements
- Define security measures

All Agents:
- Review design
- Provide feedback
- Suggest improvements
```

### 3. Implementation Phase
```markdown
Implementation Engineer:
- Develop code
- Create tests
- Implement security measures

QA Analyst:
- Review code quality
- Verify test coverage
- Validate implementation

Documentation Specialist:
- Create technical documentation
- Document APIs
- Update user guides
```

### 4. Verification Phase
```markdown
QA Analyst:
- Conduct testing
- Verify requirements
- Validate security

Implementation Engineer:
- Address issues
- Optimize performance
- Finalize implementation

Documentation Specialist:
- Complete documentation
- Update changelog
- Prepare release notes
```

## Handoff Protocol

### Handoff Template
```markdown
[HANDOFF FROM: Agent Role]

# Completed Work
- [List completed tasks]
- [Include results and metrics]

# Current Status
- [Implementation state]
- [Outstanding issues]
- [Blocking items]

# Context References
- [Key files]
- [Important decisions]
- [Related documentation]

# Next Steps
- [Tasks for next agent]
- [Priority order]
- [Dependencies]

[HANDOFF TO: Next Agent Role]
```

